              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Baking Nana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love ham that tastes like HAM. I would suggest using a Turkey sized oven bag to heat the ham - it really protects the meat and keeps it moist."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alana Johnson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I find this to be a good recipe to build on. I mixed the chicken broth with gravy, pepper and garlic and cooked at a lower temperature for a longer time and it came out great. Of all the food I made for Thanksgiving (not including dessert), this was the most popular.",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-25T15:44:19.687Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Leslie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm trying to cut the sugar use in our home and this recipe was perfect for that. We enjoy ham but not all of the sugary sweetness of a glaze. I cooked a 9 lb. ham using chicken broth except I cooked it at 325 for 2 1/2 hours. The meat came out tender and delicious . I saved the juices in the refrigerator, scraped the fat off the top and will use the remaining juices, along with the bone, for a pot of soup. Thanks for a great and simple recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-12T20:28:44.880Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Patrick H"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used the slow cooker instead. I put in the broth, then the ham. I had to make a few adjustments, but it still worked fine. My wife is diabetic, so we can't do the sugar thing",
            "datePublished": "2018-04-01T17:25:30.343Z"
          },
